# tools/cl/click_order_witness.rish -- the TWO-CLICK READING-ORDER relation on metal: turn TWO points into TWO whole-group selections, then read
# which group a surface would present FIRST on the page, lifting image/reading_order.rye's per-object rank from the OBJECT to the GROUP through
# image/hit_test.rye and image/overlap_clusters.rye's cluster_of (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/click_relation.rye reads how two tapped groups sit in SPACE (same-group, true gap, frame overlap). This
# rung reads how they sit in the reading SEQUENCE: image/hit_test.rye names the ONE object under a point, image/overlap_clusters.rye's cluster_of names
# the connected group that object belongs to, and image/reading_order.rye seats every object in one total top-to-bottom, left-to-right page order. A
# group reads at the rank of its FIRST-appearing member -- a reading over readings, no plane of its own, no pixel written.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a group's reading order is a PROJECTION of the object order down to whole groups, coarser than it and NOT
# recoverable from the two tapped objects' own ranks. Over a scene whose object reading order is [P1, Q, P2] with P1 and P2 one connected group G1 and
# the block Q a distinct group G2 reading BETWEEN them: tapping P1 (rank 1) or P2 (rank 3) both read the group's min rank 1 and lead label 1 (invariant
# to the tap site); tapping P2 then Q reads the group order G1-before-G2 TRUE while the two tapped OBJECTS read the opposite (Q before P2), so the group
# order interleaves the object order and only each group's MINIMUM decides; a group never reads before itself (SameGroup); a background tap refuses
# EmptyClick; a point off the map refuses PointOutOfBounds; determinism. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cl/click_order_witness.rish

say "click_order: Language EN -- Season G two-click reading-order; a group reads at its FIRST member's rank, so the group order is a projection of the object order that can DISAGREE with the two tapped objects' own ranks; NO float, NO tolerance."
say "click_order: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the click-to-group resolution and the group-rank reduction; hit_test owns the point-to-object arbiter, overlap_clusters owns cluster_of (the object-to-group map), reading_order owns reading_rank and the total-order comparator. No plane of its own, no pixel written -- a reading over readings."
say "click_order: Lens TAME -- each click resolves to at most one label through the hit test, the group-rank scan walks the object count bounded by scene_graph_max_objects; a background tap refuses EmptyClick, a point off the map refuses PointOutOfBounds having read nothing, a group weighed against itself refuses SameGroup; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/click_order"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/click_order.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "click_order: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "click_order: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "click_order: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-click-order" else "click_order: selftest did not print the GREEN line"
assert selftest.out contains "the TWO-CLICK READING-ORDER relation" else "click_order: the two-click-order claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a group's reading order is a PROJECTION of the object order" else "click_order: the decisive crux did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "WHERE YOU TAP WITHIN A GROUP NEVER CHANGES THE GROUP'S PLACE" else "click_order: the invariance claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "THE GROUP ORDER DISAGREES WITH THE TAPPED-OBJECT ORDER" else "click_order: the projection claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a strict total order over groups" else "click_order: the total-order claim did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "refuses SameGroup by name" else "click_order: the SameGroup refusal did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the same pair reads the same order twice" else "click_order: determinism did not print"

say "click_order: GREEN on metal -- the two-click reading-order relation, two taps resolving to two whole groups then read for which reads first on the page, a group reading at its first member's rank so the relation is invariant to the tap site, the group order projecting and interleaving the object order and disagreeing with the tapped objects' own ranks, refusals by name, determinism. Season G open-media."
